      "thinking": "The real fault is that io-shop calls the pricing service synchronously on the render path with no timeout or deadline, so any slowness downstream becomes a full outage for every request. The fix is to add a deadline/budget so the shop can fail gracefully instead of hanging indefinitely.\n\nI notice basket_total sits inside the try block in serve_account_page, so if pricing fails or hangs, the whole page fails along with it \u2014 no partial rendering happens. What's really needed is a deadline: if the pricing call exceeds a time budget, the page should render without the basket total rather than blocking indefinitely, but the shop has no mechanism to abort or timeout the call itself since it only measures duration after the fact.\n\nAdding a timeout parameter to the pricing seam's signature would break too many existing callers and tests, so I should look for another angle. Let me search across the repo for every caller of basket_total to understand how widely it's used before deciding on a fix.\n\n",
